{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"I had to take possession of the [illegible/abbreviated term], in order to encounter it. — Then a walk along the old, familiar paths of the beautiful park, trodden 25 years ago, greeting the banks of the little Ilm and its quieter waves, which have heard many an immortal song. At 2 o’clock to lunch at Goethe’s, which was excellent and honored by the best appetite; — Mrs. von Goethe!) is, expecting her delivery every hour, invisible, — so she was not at the table, — the sister, Miss von Pogwisch), quite lively, Court Councillor Vogel the doctor, a Mr. Emmerich), Goethe’s secretary, the two grandchildren, the son, Zelter and I — I sat next to Goethe, on my right the aforementioned Miss; the Weimar guests quieter, but we cheerful, conversational, eating and drinking bravely, — I had to tell Goethe a great deal about the political and literary views and interests in France, he was very interested in everything; he is quite strong, healthy, generally the old, i.e. always young — somewhat quieter — such a venerable, good, faithful head, that one forgets the great man of genius and inexhaustible energy of talent; we are as old, faithful friends anyway not on the footing of observation, — how he appears or what he has spoken, but cordially together, and not for the sake of boasting and honor, that of having seen and heard him, etc. — The son told me very explicitly after the meal how Goethe had rejoiced in the hope that I would call on him on my return journey from Paris; he spoke to me in general in detail about his relationship and feelings towards his father in every respect, and one must praise Goethe in his age and way of life as happy, knowing him in such love and care, and respect and love the son for it. This evening I was then also at the theater, — and now I am writing this to you, — and what I have principally to add is about our plans or rather decisions, finally to go home. Goethe would therefore have Zelter and me with him at least tomorrow; so we travel the day after tomorrow; Zelter just as satisfied that I am with him, as I am that he makes the further journey with me. But since we are both old gentlemen by now and convenience is agreeable and useful to us, we are not inclined to the bravery of the express post,... but we will depart on Friday with the hired coach, which we have already hired, and, if God wills, arrive at your place on Sunday, where your Odysseus, after the multicolored voyages, will return to the monochromaticity of domestic life (returning!) to embrace you."}}],"created":1795220885,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":586,"prompt_tokens":747,"total_tokens":1333,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-GEC0PrU0wGr8RmDzz6iNIvaiU2YuGfE6","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":747,"prompt_ms":810.123,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0845020080321286,"prompt_per_second":922.0822023322384,"predicted_n":586,"predicted_ms":13691.854,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.40487863247863,"predicted_per_second":42.72613482439997}}